Test Cases Document (updated per validation feedback)
US-1: Handle customer inquiries
TC-1.1 — Respond to a received inquiry (success)
Preconditions: A customer inquiry exists and is received.
Steps:
Open the received inquiry.
Enter a response.
Send the response.
Expected result:
The response is sent successfully.
The inquiry is updated with the sent response.
TC-1.2 — Attempt to send an empty response (failure / edge)
Preconditions: A customer inquiry exists and is received.
Steps:
Open the inquiry.
Leave response content empty.
Attempt to send the response.
Expected result:
The system does not send an empty response (send action fails or is not allowed).
The inquiry is not updated with an empty response.
TC-1.3 — Attempt to respond when inquiry cannot be opened (failure / edge)
Preconditions: An inquiry exists but is not accessible/openable.
Steps:
Attempt to open the inquiry.
Expected result:
The inquiry does not open successfully.
A response cannot be sent for that inquiry in this state.
US-2: Retrieve CRM context needed for handling
TC-2.1 — Retrieve CRM info for an inquiry requiring context (success)
Preconditions: An inquiry is open and requires customer/account context.
Steps:
Request CRM information for the inquiry.
View the returned CRM information.
Expected result:
The customer/account information needed to address the inquiry is retrieved from the CRM.
Retrieved CRM information is viewable within the current inquiry handling session.
TC-2.2 — CRM returns no matching customer/account data (failure / edge)
Preconditions: Inquiry is open; CRM has no matching record for the inquiry context.
Steps:
Request CRM information.
Expected result:
The system indicates that no CRM information is available for the inquiry.
No CRM information is shown as retrieved/available for the current session.
TC-2.3 — CRM access fails during retrieval (failure / edge)
Preconditions: Inquiry is open; CRM is unavailable or the request fails.
Steps:
Request CRM information.
Expected result:
The system indicates the CRM retrieval failed.
CRM information is not shown as retrieved/available for the current session.
TC-2.4 — CRM info remains available within the same inquiry handling session (success)
Preconditions: Inquiry is open; CRM info was retrieved successfully earlier in the same session.
Steps:
Navigate within the inquiry handling session (e.g., move away from the CRM view/section and return).
View CRM information again.
Expected result:
Previously retrieved CRM information remains available within the same inquiry handling session.
TC-2.5 — CRM info is not assumed available across sessions (edge / boundary)
Preconditions: CRM info was retrieved successfully in a prior inquiry handling session.
Steps:
End the current inquiry handling session.
Reopen the same inquiry in a new inquiry handling session.
Check CRM information availability without requesting retrieval again.
Expected result:
CRM information is not assumed available in the new session unless retrieved again in that session (or the system clearly indicates its current-session availability state).
US-3: Use CRM context while responding
TC-3.1 — Send a response incorporating CRM context (success)
Preconditions: Inquiry is open; CRM information is available for the inquiry.
Steps:
Draft a response that uses the available CRM context.
Send the response.
Expected result:
The response is sent successfully while CRM context is available to support the response.
The inquiry is updated with the sent response.
TC-3.2 — Send a response when CRM context is not available (edge)
Preconditions: Inquiry is open; no CRM information is retrieved/available in the current session.
Steps:
Draft a response.
Send the response.
Expected result:
The response is sent successfully without CRM context.
No CRM information is shown as available for this inquiry handling session.
TC-3.3 — Retrieve CRM info again during inquiry handling (success)
Preconditions: Inquiry is open; additional CRM context is needed during handling.
Steps:
Request CRM information again during the same inquiry handling session.
View the returned CRM information.
Expected result:
CRM information can be retrieved again during inquiry handling.
Retrieved CRM information is viewable within the current session.
US-4: Support issue resolution
TC-4.1 — Progress interaction toward resolution using inquiry details and CRM context (success)
Preconditions: Inquiry is open; a customer issue is identified; CRM context may or may not be available.
Steps:
Handle the inquiry using available inquiry details.
If CRM context is available, use it during handling.
Proceed until the issue is addressed.
Expected result:
The interaction is progressed toward resolution using the available inquiry details and (when available) CRM context.
TC-4.2 — Mark inquiry as resolved/closed when issue is addressed (success)
Preconditions: Inquiry is open; issue is addressed.
Steps:
Conclude the interaction.
Expected result:
The inquiry is marked as resolved/closed.
TC-4.3 — Attempt to mark inquiry resolved/closed when issue is not addressed (failure / edge)
Preconditions: Inquiry is open; issue is not addressed.
Steps:
Attempt to conclude the interaction as resolved/closed.
Expected result:
The system does not mark the inquiry as resolved/closed when the issue is not addressed (close-as-resolved fails or is not allowed).
